{#- The folded "Source code in" block of a function, kept out of the site search.

mkdocstrings' own template, with its source block inside an element the
search plugin of Material skips (data-search-exclude). The source is still
on the page. Without this the search index is mostly function source, and a
search for an ordinary word finds source ahead of the documentation.

The element is a <section> because the search plugin tells elements apart
by tag name alone: around a <div>, the first <div> that closes inside the
source block ends the exclusion, and the source is indexed after all.
tests/test_api_docs.py holds this file and its line in .mkdocs.yml.
-#}
{% extends "_base/function.html.jinja" %}

{% block source scoped %}
  <section data-search-exclude>
    {{ super() }}
  </section>
{% endblock source %}
